---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="A release you cannot recall" hint="Thirty days after version 7 ships to 1,000,000 active users in store stages of 1%, 5%, 20%, 50% and 100%. Assumptions: 8% of users never update and 5% have a phone too old for it; each day 15% of the users the store has offered it to install it; 0.5% of users crash on any healthy version; a gate halts when the new version is worse by more than 0.3 points; day 0 is a Thursday. A simple model, not a real store.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Start with the defaults: a <b>Crash in the new build</b> hitting <b>3%</b> of its users, <b>No monitoring</b>, <b>New build only</b> and a <b>Hotfix review delay (days)</b> of <b>3</b>. Only support tickets notice, so <b>6,424</b> users hit the bug, the fix is out on day <b>14</b> and the bug is contained on day <b>23</b>, with <b>8,513</b> users still on the broken version. Set <b>Monitoring</b> to <b>Daily review, weekdays</b>: <b>1,133</b> users hit it. Set it to <b>Automatic gate</b>: only <b>72</b> do, and it is contained on day <b>13</b>.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Hotfix review delay (days)</b> to <b>7</b>: the hotfix is out on day <b>10</b> instead of day 6, the bug is contained on day <b>17</b>, and <b>898</b> user-days are spent with it. Now set <b>Bug in the new version</b> to <b>Bug behind a server flag</b> and <b>Kill mechanism</b> to <b>Server flag</b>: it is contained on day 2, the same <b>72</b> users hit it, only <b>111</b> user-days are spent with it, and <b>0</b> users are left on a broken version. Set <b>Bug in the new version</b> back to <b>Crash in the new build</b> and the flag helps nobody.</li>
    <li>The backfire of a small gate. Set <b>Bug in the new version</b> to <b>None, a healthy release</b>, <b>Monitoring</b> to <b>Automatic gate</b> and <b>Gate sample size</b> to <b>200 users</b>: noise halts the release <b>6</b> times, the store reaches 100% only on day <b>19</b>, and just <b>527,717</b> users have v7 after 30 days. Set <b>Gate sample size</b> to <b>20,000 users</b> and <b>844,582</b> do. Put the crash back, with <b>Bug in the new version</b> set to <b>Crash in the new build</b>: a gate that big waits for the 20% stage and <b>1,133</b> users hit the bug.</li>
    <li>The backfire of a high minimum version. Set <b>Monitoring</b> to <b>Automatic gate</b>, <b>Gate sample size</b> to <b>2,000 users</b> and <b>Minimum supported version on day 14</b> to <b>v5 and above</b>: <b>23,401</b> users are locked out. Set it to <b>v7 only</b>: <b>130,003</b> users are locked out, the 13% who cannot or will not update.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg mrr" data-mrr>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Bug in the new version <select class="pg-in" data-bug><option value="none">None, a healthy release</option><option value="crash" selected>Crash in the new build</option><option value="flag">Bug behind a server flag</option></select></label>
      <label>Users the bug hits <select class="pg-in" data-pm><option value="10">1%</option><option value="30" selected>3%</option><option value="100">10%</option></select></label>
      <label>Monitoring <select class="pg-in" data-mon><option value="none" selected>No monitoring, tickets and reviews</option><option value="review">Daily review, weekdays</option><option value="gate">Automatic gate</option></select></label>
      <label>Gate sample size <select class="pg-in" data-sample><option value="200">200 users</option><option value="2000" selected>2,000 users</option><option value="20000">20,000 users</option></select></label>
      <label>Kill mechanism <select class="pg-in" data-kill><option value="build" selected>New build only</option><option value="flag">Server flag</option></select></label>
      <RangeField label="Hotfix review delay (days)" name="delay" min="0" max="7" value="3" />
      <label>Minimum supported version on day 14 <select class="pg-in" data-floor><option value="none" selected>No minimum</option><option value="v5">v5 and above</option><option value="v6">v6 and above</option><option value="v7">v7 only</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Users who hit the bug</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Bug contained</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Store rollout</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>Still on the broken version</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" data-b5 style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Version mix after 30 days</h3>
      <div class="mrr-mix" data-mix role="img" aria-label="Share of the 1,000,000 users on each version after 30 days"></div>
      <ul class="mrr-legend" data-legend></ul>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Each day: users still hitting the bug, and the share who have the new version</h3>
      <div class="mrr-chart" data-chart role="img" aria-label="Users hitting the bug each day and the share of users on the new version, for 30 days"></div>
      <div class="mrr-marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <span class="pg-note">Columns: users who are on a build with the bug and affected by it that day, relative to the tallest column of this run. Dots: share of the 1,000,000 users who have the new version, out of 100%. Marks: the day the stop is in force, and the day the hotfix is out.</span>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatThousands } from '../../playground';
  // The same model as the code samples, plus a record of every day for the chart.
  const DAYS = 30, USERS = 1000000;
  const OLD_MIX = [600000, 220000, 180000];
  const STUCK_PCT = 13, ORGANIC_PCT = 15, HOTFIX_PCT = 25, STICKY_PCT = 3, FORCED_PCT = 70;
  const FLOOR_DAY = 14, FIX_DAYS = 1, HALT_DAYS = 3, BASE_PM = 5, MARGIN_PM = 3, TICKETS = 3000, TICKET_LAG = 3, REVIEW_MIN = 5000, SEED = 20261120;
  const stageAt = (u: number) => (u < 2 ? 1 : u < 4 ? 5 : u < 7 ? 20 : u < 10 ? 50 : 100);
  const weekday = (d: number) => (d + 3) % 7 < 5;
  interface Opts { bug: string; bugPm: number; monitor: string; sample: number; kill: string; delay: number; floor: string }

  function simulate({ bug, bugPm, monitor, sample, kill, delay, floor }: Opts) {
    let rng = SEED;
    const rand = () => (rng = (rng * 48271) % 2147483647);
    const W = OLD_MIX.map((c) => Math.floor((c * (100 - STUCK_PCT)) / 100));
    const S = OLD_MIX.map((c, i) => c - W[i]);
    const U = W.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
    const blocked = floor === 'v5' ? [2] : floor === 'v6' ? [1, 2] : floor === 'v7' ? [0, 1, 2] : [];
    const flagRoute = bug === 'flag' && kill === 'flag';
    let nV7 = 0, nFix = 0, adopted = 0, hits = 0, aff = 0, bugDays = 0, lockedStuck = 0, sticky = 0;
    let stage = 0, unfrozen = 0, F = -1, H = -1, freezeUntil = 0, falseHalts = 0, full = -1;
    const suffer: number[] = [], endNew: number[] = [], endAff: number[] = [];
    for (let d = 0; d < DAYS; d++) {
      if (flagRoute && F >= 0 && d >= F) aff = 0;
      if (monitor === 'review' && F < 0 && bug !== 'none' && weekday(d) && d > 0) {
        if (endNew[d - 1] >= REVIEW_MIN && 1000 * endAff[d - 1] >= BASE_PM * endNew[d - 1]) F = d + 1;
      }
      if (F >= 0 && !flagRoute && H < 0) H = F + FIX_DAYS + delay;
      const halted = d < freezeUntil || (F >= 0 && !flagRoute && d >= F && d < H);
      if (d === H) sticky = Math.floor((nV7 * STICKY_PCT) / 100);
      if (H >= 0 && d >= H) {
        const mig = Math.floor(((nV7 - sticky) * HOTFIX_PCT) / 100);
        if (nV7 > 0) aff = Math.floor((aff * (nV7 - mig)) / nV7);
        nV7 -= mig; nFix += mig;
      }
      if (H >= 0 && d >= H) stage = 100;
      else if (!halted) { stage = stageAt(unfrozen); unfrozen++; }
      if (stage === 100 && full < 0) full = d;
      const adopt = (x: number) => {
        if (x <= 0) return;
        adopted += x;
        if (H >= 0 && d >= H) { nFix += x; return; }
        nV7 += x;
        if (bug !== 'none' && !(flagRoute && F >= 0 && d >= F)) { const a = Math.floor((x * bugPm) / 1000); hits += a; aff += a; }
      };
      if (d === FLOOR_DAY) for (const b of blocked) { lockedStuck += S[b]; S[b] = 0; }
      if (d >= FLOOR_DAY && !halted && stage === 100) {
        for (const b of blocked) { const m = Math.floor((W[b] * FORCED_PCT) / 100); W[b] -= m; adopt(m); }
      }
      if (!halted) {
        const sumW = W.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
        const want = Math.min(sumW, Math.floor(((Math.floor((U * stage) / 100) - adopted) * ORGANIC_PCT) / 100));
        if (want > 0) {
          let given = 0;
          const take = W.map((w) => { const t = Math.floor((want * w) / sumW); given += t; return t; });
          for (let b = 0; b < 3 && given < want; b++) { const e = Math.min(W[b] - take[b], want - given); take[b] += e; given += e; }
          for (let b = 0; b < 3; b++) W[b] -= take[b];
          adopt(want);
        }
      }
      suffer.push(aff); endNew.push(nV7 + nFix); endAff.push(aff); bugDays += aff;
      if (F < 0 && bug !== 'none' && monitor === 'none' && hits >= TICKETS) F = d + TICKET_LAG;
      if (F < 0 && monitor === 'gate' && nV7 + nFix >= sample && d >= freezeUntil) {
        const pm = BASE_PM * 1000 + Math.floor((aff * 1000000) / (nV7 + nFix));
        let c = 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < sample; i++) if (rand() % 1000000 < pm) c++;
        if (c * 1000 > sample * (BASE_PM + MARGIN_PM)) {
          if (aff > 0) F = d + 1;
          else { freezeUntil = d + 1 + HALT_DAYS; falseHalts++; }
        }
      }
    }
    let peak = 0, contained = -1;
    suffer.forEach((s, d) => { if (s > peak) { peak = s; contained = -1; } else if (contained < 0 && s * 10 < peak) contained = d; });
    const liveBug = bug !== 'none' && !(flagRoute && F >= 0);
    const locked = lockedStuck + blocked.reduce((a, b) => a + W[b], 0);
    const old = W.map((w, i) => (blocked.includes(i) ? 0 : w) + S[i]);
    if (nV7 + nFix + old[0] + old[1] + old[2] + locked !== USERS) throw new Error('users lost');
    return { hits, bugDays, contained, full, falseHalts, F, H, flagRoute, broken: liveBug ? nV7 : 0, nV7, nFix, old, locked, suffer, peak, endNew };
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-mrr]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const chartEl = q('[data-chart]'), marksEl = q('[data-marks]');
    const cols = Array.from({ length: DAYS }, () => {
      const c = document.createElement('span'); c.className = 'mrr-col';
      const bar = document.createElement('span'); bar.className = 'mrr-bar';
      const dot = document.createElement('span'); dot.className = 'mrr-dot';
      c.append(bar, dot); chartEl.appendChild(c);
      const m = document.createElement('span'); m.className = 'mrr-mark'; marksEl.appendChild(m);
      return { c, bar, dot, m };
    });
    const MIX = [
      { name: 'v7, the new version', colour: 'var(--role-1)' }, { name: 'v7.1, the fix', colour: 'var(--good)' }, { name: 'v6', colour: 'var(--role-2)' },
      { name: 'v5', colour: 'var(--role-3)' }, { name: 'v4 or older', colour: 'var(--role-4)' }, { name: 'locked out', colour: 'var(--bad)' },
    ];
    const mixEl = q('[data-mix]'), legendEl = q('[data-legend]');
    const segs = MIX.map((m) => {
      const s = document.createElement('span'); s.className = 'mrr-seg'; s.style.background = m.colour; mixEl.appendChild(s);
      const li = document.createElement('li'); const sw = document.createElement('i'); sw.style.background = m.colour; const tx = document.createElement('span'); li.append(sw, tx); legendEl.appendChild(li);
      return { s, tx };
    });
    const box = (n: number, colour: string) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${n}]`).style.setProperty('--c', colour);
    const pct = (n: number) => `${Math.round((n * 100) / USERS)}%`;
    function draw() {
      const bug = sel('[data-bug]'), kill = sel('[data-kill]'), monitor = sel('[data-mon]');
      q('[data-delayval]').textContent = String(val('[data-delay]'));
      const r = simulate({ bug, bugPm: Number(sel('[data-pm]')), monitor, sample: Number(sel('[data-sample]')), kill, delay: val('[data-delay]'), floor: sel('[data-floor]') });
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = bug === 'none' ? 'no bug' : formatThousands(r.hits);
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = bug === 'none' ? 'a healthy release' : `of ${formatThousands(USERS)} active users; ${formatThousands(r.bugDays)} user-days spent with the bug`;
      box(1, bug === 'none' || r.hits < 100 ? 'var(--good)' : r.hits < 1000 ? 'var(--role-3)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = bug === 'none' ? 'no bug' : r.contained < 0 ? 'not within 30 days' : `day ${r.contained}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = bug === 'none' ? 'nothing to contain' : r.F < 0 ? 'nobody noticed the bug in 30 days'
        : r.flagRoute ? `flag switched off, in force on day ${r.F}` : `rollout halted on day ${r.F}, fixed build out on day ${r.H}`;
      box(2, bug === 'none' || (r.contained >= 0 && r.contained <= 7) ? 'var(--good)' : r.contained >= 0 && r.contained <= 20 ? 'var(--role-3)' : 'var(--bad)');
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = r.full < 0 ? 'not at 100%' : `100% on day ${r.full}`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = r.falseHalts ? `halted ${r.falseHalts} times by noise, ${r.falseHalts * HALT_DAYS} days frozen for nothing` : 'no false halts';
      box(3, r.falseHalts ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = formatThousands(r.broken);
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = r.broken ? 'users on a build where the bug is still live' : bug === 'none' ? 'no broken version' : 'nobody is on a build where the bug is live';
      box(4, r.broken === 0 ? 'var(--good)' : r.broken < 1000 ? 'var(--role-3)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const counts = [r.nV7, r.nFix, r.old[0], r.old[1], r.old[2], r.locked];
      counts.forEach((n, i) => {
        segs[i].s.style.flexGrow = String(n); segs[i].s.style.display = n ? '' : 'none';
        segs[i].tx.textContent = `${MIX[i].name}: ${formatThousands(n)} (${pct(n)})`;
      });
      box(5, r.locked >= USERS / 20 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');
      const peak = Math.max(1, r.peak);
      cols.forEach((col, d) => {
        col.bar.style.height = `${(r.suffer[d] * 100) / peak}%`;
        col.dot.style.bottom = `${(r.endNew[d] * 100) / USERS}%`;
        col.m.textContent = d === r.F ? 'stop' : d === r.H ? 'fix' : '';
        col.c.title = `Day ${d}: ${formatThousands(r.suffer[d])} users hitting the bug, ${pct(r.endNew[d])} have the new version`;
      });
      const v = q('[data-verdict]');
      const bad = r.hits >= 1000 || r.falseHalts > 0 || r.locked >= USERS / 20 || (bug !== 'none' && r.contained < 0);
      v.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      v.textContent = r.locked >= USERS / 20 ? `A minimum version that high locked out ${formatThousands(r.locked)} users who cannot update.`
        : bug === 'none' ? (r.falseHalts ? 'A healthy release was stopped by noise, and most users stayed on the old version.' : monitor === 'gate' ? 'A healthy release, and the gate stayed quiet.' : 'A healthy release, and nothing needed doing.')
        : r.F < 0 ? 'The bug was never noticed.'
        : bug === 'crash' && kill === 'flag' ? 'The crash is in code with no flag, so the flag did nothing and the fix had to go through the store.'
        : r.flagRoute ? 'The flag switched the bug off within a day, without a new build.'
        : r.hits >= 1000 ? 'Too many users got the broken build before anything stopped it.'
        : 'The rollout was halted early, and the fix reached phones through the store.';
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .mrr-chart { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(30, 1fr); gap: 2px; height: 120px; align-items: end; }
  .playground .mrr-col { position: relative; height: 100%; }
  .playground .mrr-bar { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; background: var(--bad); border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0; opacity: .8; }
  .playground .mrr-dot { position: absolute; left: 50%; width: 6px; height: 6px; margin: 0 0 -3px -3px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--text); }
  .playground .mrr-marks { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(30, 1fr); gap: 2px; height: 1.2em; font-size: .62rem; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--muted); }
  .playground .mrr-mark { overflow: visible; white-space: nowrap; text-align: center; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text); }
  .playground .mrr-mix { display: flex; height: 22px; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; background: var(--surface-2); margin: .4rem 0; }
  .playground .mrr-seg { min-width: 2px; }
  .playground .mrr-legend { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .25rem 1rem; font-size: .85rem; }
  .playground .mrr-legend li { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .playground .mrr-legend i { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 2px; display: inline-block; flex: none; }
</style>
